{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalReeb","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalReeb","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.kernel_horizontal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.kernel_horizontal","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L76-L76","doc":"**Kernel** (property 3):\nHorizontal forms are the kernel of contraction with ξ:\n`Ω^k_H(A) = ker(ι_ξ)`.\n\nEncoded as: the vertical projection is idempotent, and\ncontracting with ξ then re-embedding via `d` lands in the\nvertical subspace.  Together with `vertical_generator`, this\nmeans `ι_ξ` is zero on horizontal forms and non-zero on\nvertical forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.normalisation","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L66-L66","doc":"**Normalisation** (property 2):\n`θ_A(ξ) = id_𝟙`. Applying ξ then θ yields the same result\nas applying θ directly, encoding that ξ is a unit section of θ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.vertical_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.vertical_generator","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L62-L62","doc":"**Vertical generator** (property 1):\n`π_V ∘ d = ι_ξ(dθ_A)`.\nEncoded without 2-forms as: the vertical-then-contract path\nrecovers ξ.  That is, for any `f : A`, taking `d(f)`, projecting\nto the vertical subspace, then contracting with ξ yields `ξ(f)`:\n\n  `d ≫ π_V ≫ ι_ξ = ξ`\n\nThis is non-trivial: it connects `d`, `π_V`, `ι_ξ`, and `ξ`.\nThe full encoding `π_V ∘ d = ι_ξ(dθ_A)` additionally requires\n`Ω²(A)` and `d` on forms (see HigherForms). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.contract_xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.contract_xi","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The interior product (contraction) `ι_ξ : Ω¹(A) → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.d","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The differential `d : A → Ω¹(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.proj_V","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V : Ω¹(A) → Ω¹(A)` (non-zero weight\ncomponent under the torus action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.theta","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The canonical 1-form `θ_A`, abstractly a morphism `A → 𝟙`\ndual to `ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.xi","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The Reeb derivation `ξ : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.forms","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The object of 1-forms `Ω¹(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.A","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.mk","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.lean#L21-L77","doc":"**Categorical Reeb derivation**.\n\nThe endomorphism `ξ : A → A` generating the `T`-action on the\nFrobenius–Hopf object `A`.  It is equipped with a canonical 1-form\n`θ_A` (the dual of `ξ`) satisfying:\n\n1. **Vertical generator**: `π_V ∘ d = ξ ⌟ dθ_A`\n2. **Normalisation**: `θ_A(ξ) = id_𝟙`\n3. **Kernel**: `Ω^k_H(A) = ker(ξ ⌟)`\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-reeb}`\nRef: [witten1988] https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01223371 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-reeb","label":"def:categorical-reeb","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}